    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The security process at Eurostar stations is designed to be as efficient and streamlined as possible, especially during busy travel periods. At T/1 St Pancras station, the security check procedure is quick. Passengers can generally expect to wait for about 15 minutes, although this can vary based on the time of day and volume of passengers.\n\nYou're required to weigh and scan your bags at a security counter. The process is relatively quick, usually taking just a minute or so per bag, and you can watch while your bags are being checked. You can also walk right through the scanners if you prefer to keep your travel documents to hand.\n\nRegarding the station layout, there's no place you'll be stuck in unusual corridors or dark tunnels. Security checkpoints are located in well-lit, main areas of the station, and you're guided smoothly from check-in counters to your departure gates. If at any time you feel overwhelmed or need assistance, station staff are always ready to help you navigate the security process effectively.\n\nGood travel, and remember, while there might be some waiting involved, it’s typically not as long or as stressful as you might imagine. Thanks for your patience and good luck with your meeting in Paris!",
